<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/gulf-pier-sunset.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/gulf-pier-sunset-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/gulf-pier-sunset.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Biloxi</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Gulf Coast</p><h1>Biloxi Property Claim Appraisal, From Point Cadet to Woolmarket</h1><p class="lede">Biloxi has taken direct hits from Camille, Katrina and Nate, and every one left behind arguments over what repairs really cost. If your carrier’s estimate is short, appraisal may be the quickest fair way to settle it.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Harrison County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>Gulf Coast</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>East Biloxi</li><li>Point Cadet</li><li>Back Bay</li><li>West Biloxi</li><li>Woolmarket</li><li>Downtown Biloxi</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Biloxi’s housing ranges from historic cottages and shotgun houses in East Biloxi to raised post-Katrina rebuilds, mid-century homes near Keesler, and newer subdivisions north of the Back Bay in Woolmarket.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Aug 17, 1969</b><span>Hurricane Camille’s Category 5 landfall to the west</span></li><li><b>Aug 29, 2005</b><span>Hurricane Katrina’s catastrophic surge and wind</span></li><li><b>Oct 2017</b><span>Hurricane Nate’s Category 1 landfall near Biloxi</span></li><li><b>Oct 28, 2020</b><span>Hurricane Zeta’s wind across the Coast</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Hurricane surge and wind along the beachfront and Back Bay</li><li>Wind-driven rain through roofs and windows</li><li>Split wind and homeowners policy disputes</li><li>Commercial and hospitality property losses</li><li>Mold after delayed water mitigation</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Biloxi’s storm record</h2>
<p>Biloxi shares county-seat status in Harrison County with Gulfport and sits on a peninsula between the Mississippi Sound and the Back Bay. Water on two sides means storms hit from more than one direction.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hurricane Camille, August 17, 1969:</strong> a Category 5 landfall to the west near Pass Christian and Bay St. Louis, with heavy damage in Biloxi.</li>
<li><strong>Hurricane Katrina, August 29, 2005:</strong> surge swept East Biloxi and Point Cadet and pushed into the Back Bay, while wind damaged roofs across the city.</li>
<li><strong>Hurricane Nate, October 2017:</strong> a Category 1 landfall near Biloxi, with surge along the beachfront and wind damage to roofs and signs.</li>
<li><strong>Hurricane Zeta, October 28, 2020:</strong> landfall in Louisiana, but strong wind across the whole Mississippi Coast.</li>
</ul>
<p>Katrina in particular left a long trail of wind-versus-water fights. Those coverage questions are outside what appraisal decides, but the dollar amount of each piece of damage is not.</p>

<h2>East Biloxi, Point Cadet and the rest of the city</h2>
<p>East Biloxi and Point Cadet are the city’s oldest neighborhoods, with cottages, shotgun houses and seafood-industry roots. Many lots there were rebuilt after 2005, often raised. West Biloxi and the areas around Keesler Air Force Base hold a lot of mid-century homes and rentals. Woolmarket, north of the Back Bay, is newer and more suburban. Downtown Biloxi mixes older commercial buildings with newer construction.</p>
<p>Biloxi is also a hospitality city. The casino resorts and hotels along the beach and the Back Bay, plus the restaurants, shops and rental property that serve them, produce large commercial claims. For those, see our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">commercial and HOA appraisal</a> service.</p>

<h2>Common estimate gaps on Biloxi claims</h2>
<h3>Homes and rentals</h3>
<ul>
<li>Raised homes priced without the lifts, staging and extra labor they require.</li>
<li>Wind-driven rain damage written as a small ceiling patch when insulation, drywall and flooring were soaked.</li>
<li>Mold remediation limited by a policy sublimit, with the remaining tear-out left out of the estimate.</li>
<li>Older cottages with wood siding and trim profiles that standard pricing doesn’t match.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Commercial and hospitality property</h3>
<ul>
<li>Roof systems on large flat or low-slope buildings measured short or repaired in patches.</li>
<li>Exterior finishes and signage on storm-exposed buildings left off the estimate.</li>
<li>Disputes over how many units, rooms or floors a loss actually reached.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">Two policies, two deductibles</b><p>Biloxi is inside the MWUA territory. If your wind coverage is separate, expect a separate wind deductible, often a percentage of Coverage A. Run your numbers before you decide whether appraisal is worth it.</p></div>

<h2>Working a Biloxi claim through appraisal</h2>
<p>We review the carrier’s estimate, build a line-by-line scope and, if your policy has an appraisal clause and the dispute is about amount, represent you through the process. The <a href="/claim-advice/coast-hurricane-deductibles-explained/">Coast hurricane deductibles guide</a> is a good place to start before you file a demand.</p>
<p>We also serve D’Iberville and Ocean Springs across the Back Bay and the bay bridge. Confirm any deadline with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Biloxi</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Biloxi and the rest of Harrison County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/hurricane-named-storm-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Named Storm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Biloxi claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Do you handle casino, hotel and commercial claims in Biloxi?</summary><p>Yes. We work commercial, HOA and condominium claims as well as homeowner claims. Larger losses often involve more complex roof systems, multiple buildings and business owners with their own appraisal clause terms.</p></details><details><summary>I live near Keesler and rent my house out. Can I still use appraisal?</summary><p>If your landlord or dwelling policy has an appraisal clause and you and your carrier disagree on the amount of a covered loss, you can generally invoke it. Check the clause wording for notice and timing requirements.</p></details></div>
